Sval: the address bar's history group is labelled "Your History"

Firefox labels the group of rows from the user's own data, history and
bookmarks and open tabs, with its Suggest brand, which Sval's no-firefox-name
patch reduces to a bare "Suggest". The label is a Fluent string the address
bar and the home page both read, so only a patch renames it.

diff --git a/browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl b/browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl
index 3fc288109c..fb562f6b88 100644
--- a/browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl
+++ b/browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl
@@ -955,7 +955,7 @@ urlbar-view-context-menu-open-in-private-window =
 # A label shown above the "Firefox Suggest" (bookmarks/history) group in the
 # urlbar results.
 urlbar-group-firefox-suggest =
-  .label = { -firefox-suggest-brand-name }
+  .label = Your History
 
 # A label shown above the search suggestions group in the urlbar results. It
 # should use sentence case.
